{
  "course": "初中60短文",
  "passage": 52,
  "title": "Passage 52",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s52-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p01.mp3",
      "en": "The night sky is our earliest library.",
      "cn": "夜空是我们最早的图书馆。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s52-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p02.mp3",
      "en": "There, we stored our knowledge, and passed it down around the fire, before we invented the written word.",
      "cn": "在文字发明之前，我们在那里贮存知识，并在炉火旁将其代代相传。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s52-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p03.mp3",
      "en": "I remember going to the local university for an astronomy night when I was a child.",
      "cn": "我记得小时候去当地大学参加过一次天文之夜活动。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s52-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p04.mp3",
      "en": "That night, I saw Saturn, one of the planets, and its rings with my own eyes for the first time.",
      "cn": "那天晚上，我第一次亲眼看到了行星之一的土星及它的星环。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s52-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p05.mp3",
      "en": "The rings shone bright against the blackness of space and suddenly the universe wasn't something that you only read about or imagined in your head.",
      "cn": "土星环在漆黑的太空中闪闪发光，突然间，宇宙不再是只能在书中读到或在脑海中想象的事物。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s52-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p06.mp3",
      "en": "It was right there, and you were a part of it.",
      "cn": "它就在那里，而你就是其中的一部分。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s52-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p07.mp3",
      "en": "That moment is priceless.",
      "cn": "那一刻是无价的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s52-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p08.mp3",
      "en": "I admired the beauty of the stars and felt a deep connection with the night sky.",
      "cn": "我欣赏着星空之美，感受到与夜空之间有种深刻的联系。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s52-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p09.mp3",
      "en": "While starlight is good, light pollution here on Earth can be a real problem.",
      "cn": "虽然星光很好，但地球上的光污染却是真实存在的问题。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s52-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p10.mp3",
      "en": "For the past 200 years or so, we have used too much electricity to make the night brighter.",
      "cn": "在过去的大约200年间，我们使用了过多的电力来让夜晚更明亮。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s52-p11-01",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p11-01.mp3",
      "en": "In our busy cities, street lamps and city lights can block our view of the stars,",
      "cn": "在繁忙的城市中，路灯和城市灯光会遮挡我们观赏星星的视线，几乎让人无法看到它们。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s52-p11-02",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p11-02.mp3",
      "en": "making it almost impossible to see them.",
      "cn": "在繁忙的城市中，路灯和城市灯光会遮挡我们观赏星星的视线，几乎让人无法看到它们。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s52-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p12.mp3",
      "en": "Luckily, some cities have taken action, like setting up new lights along the streets that direct downwards.",
      "cn": "幸运的是，一些城市已经采取了行动，比如在街道两旁安装向下照射的新型路灯。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s52-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p13.mp3",
      "en": "I hope more cities will join in and continue the practice of controlling unnecessary lighting.",
      "cn": "我希望更多的城市能够加入进来，继续实施限制非必要照明的做法。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s52-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s52-p14.mp3",
      "en": "This way, we can enjoy the peace and beauty of the universe.",
      "cn": "这样，我们才能享受宇宙的宁静与美丽。"
    }
  ],
